{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/793616-cleansing-a-wyrm-corrupted-caern","id":793616,"title":"Cleansing a Wyrm-corrupted Caern","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-27T09:22:45-08:00","id":793616,"title":"Cleansing a Wyrm-corrupted Caern","content":"Is a rite of cleansing enough?<br /> Where do I find official W20 resource about the matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T15:27:10-08:00","id":793807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucaCherstich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/793616-cleansing-a-wyrm-corrupted-caern#post793616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a rite of cleansing enough?<br /> Where do I find official W20 resource about the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Nope, not by a long shot.<br /> 2. There is no specific ritual for this sort of thing. Caerns that have fallen to the Wyrm are not uncommon, but retaking them for Gaia is, unfortunately, quite rare.<br /> <br /> Saving a Caern from the coils of the Wyrm is a huge undertaking, one that should require a lot of steps, and could easily be the focal point of a story. The source of corruption has to be removed (whatever it was), the land has to be cleansed meticulously, and the spiritual environment has to be purified. Any and all fallen spirits squatting in the area have to be dealt with, up to and including the Caern Totem. The Caern Totem may still be saved, but this should be quite difficult and the method of redemption is highly dependent on what caused the Caern to fall in the first place, as well as the nature of the spirit in question. Permanently destroying the Caern Totem is also possible, but only if you have another spirit ready and willing to assume the mantle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-27T22:35:51-08:00","id":793968,"title":"","content":"That, plus: I would consider whether or not the Caern was originally a Gaian Caern, or if it was birthed as a corrupted Wyrm Caern. If it was one that began as Gaian rather than Wyrm, it may be possible to enlist the aid of either the current or previous Totem. If the Totem was displaced/replaced or that incarnation slain, it (or another aspect of that Totem) might be able to be brought on to reclaim its Caern. If that Totem was made corrupt and fell with the Caern, it might be brought back to its purpose, and help to cleanse the rest.<br /> <br /> But definitely, the Rite of Cleansing is not enough. When it comes to a whole Caern, that's quest material, and should depend on the details of the individual Caern and circumstances of the fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T16:59:06-08:00","id":794473,"title":"","content":"Again i'll look at trinity caern here (wonderful short story), where the spiral in question referes to the creation of the hive as using &quot;the rite of caern building.&quot; And knowing that, I'd call a fallen caern a hive, and assume you'd need a major kick in the ass to bring it back. it's far easier to taint something then it is to fix it. <br /> <br /> What is it that brings spiritual energy to the location, and is it too far gone to be remotely fixable? Those are questions I would ask. If its a nuclear test site... well no. If it was a glade that someone tainted and would represent a rank 1 hive? That would be a lot easier, but the host spirits are likely already beyond saving. Nevermind that you have to deal with horde of black spirals that certainly take up residence in the location.<br /> <br /> Hell knowing the spiral gift list from botw20th, you may have to kill everything and &quot;clense with fire&quot; before its maintainable for gaia again. Might be better to just outright destroy it and build a healthy park over it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T15:57:25-08:00","id":795146,"title":"","content":"I would say the key is in figuring out what went wrong and getting rid of its protectors. Considering the fact that this will include all the BSD's, Banes, Fomori and human agents, this may be quite the tall order. Once you do, you need to keep it safe long enough to enact a rite of legendary proportions - all the while protecting the rite and its ritemasters from hordes of Wyrmish reinformcents coming in for the slaughter.<br /> <br /> I'd say that you need to get a strong support from the spirits to help you fight in the Umbra and an army of Shifters and Kin to do the fighting. The rite itself would most likely be quite epic in the materials it would require - most likely involving something that was used in the original consecration of the Caern and rare materials that could only be found through umbral quests.<br /> <br /> If this was achieved it might actually be feasible to have a clean Caern, albeit one whose location will be well known to the agents of the Wyrm and for which the costs of reclamation will be huge. Might be easier just to level it and close it down...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T21:20:49-08:00","id":797180,"title":"","content":"Many many steps.<br /> First purge any wyrm minions hiding within the caern both umbral and tellurian<br /> Second find the former sept totem and seek to bring it back or find a new one.<br /> Begin cleansing the land and umbral landscape. Keepers of the Land and Rite Masters will be needed here<br /> Sever any wyrm moonbridge that may be attached.<br /> Begin pulling in strong healing/purity spirits as well as spirits associated to what it was before the fall<br /> Get some packs of garou within to start protecting it and fighting off any wyrm remnants that may have lingered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}